  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_type\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 3,\n  \"section_title\": \"Grammar and Vocabulary (B2)\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 21,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct translation for 'It was decided that we should leave early'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) It had been determined that I would leave late.\",\n        \"B) It had been agreed that I should leave early.\",\n        \"C) It was decided that we should leave late.\",\n        \"D) It had been planned that I would leave early.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 22,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the passive voice correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) The book was read by John.\",\n        \"B) John read the book.\",\n        \"C) It is being written a new law.\",\n        \"D) A new law has been introduced.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 23,\n      \"question\": \"Choose the appropriate advanced conditional to express 'If I had studied harder, I would have passed the exam'.\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Had I studied hard and passed the exam.\",\n        \"B) Would I have studied harder and passed the exam.\",\n        \"C) I had studied harder, and would pass the exam.\",\n        \"D) Had I studied harder, I would have passed the exam.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 24,\n      \"question\": \"Which discourse marker best connects the two sentences? 'They didn't go to the party.' 'According to him, they were sick.'\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) However.\",\n        \"B) Therefore.\",\n        \"C) Nevertheless.\",\n        \"D) So.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 25,\n      \"question\": \"Which collocation is incorrect?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) on the other hand\",\n        \"B) at best\",\n        \"C) behind schedule\",\n        \"D) ahead of time\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent preposition is used incorrectly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) because of\",\n        \"B) thanks to\",\n        \"C) apart from\",\n        \"D) instead of\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Choose the most precise lexical choice for 'The results showed that he had been injured.'\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) was hurt.\",\n        \"B) got hurt.\",\n        \"C) suffered an injury.\",\n        \"D) had a mishap.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses reported speech correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) 'I think it's going to rain.' she said.\",\n        \"B) 'She says I should leave early.' he replied.\",\n        \"C) 'They are playing football.' they were informed.\",\n        \"D) 'It's going to rain.' she said.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is an incorrect use of 'even though'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Even though it was raining, we went for a walk.\",\n        \"B) Despite the heavy traffic, I arrived on time.\",\n        \"C) Although she didn't like him, they became friends.\",\n        \"D) Even though it was cold, we decided to stay outside.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence demonstrates the use of a subordinating conjunction correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I will call you when he arrives.\",\n        \"B) She went to the store because she was hungry.\",\n        \"C) The book is interesting even though it's long.\",\n        \"D) I will finish my homework if you help me.\"\n      ]\n    }\n}\n```",
